Upstream attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Laya (multilingual checkpoint)
   Provider : Convai Innovations
   Source   : https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
   License  : Apache License 2.0
   Role     : base model for this fine-tune (encoder + decision head)

2. mmBERT-base
   Provider : JHU CLSP
   Source   : https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base
   License  : Apache License 2.0
   Role     : encoder backbone of Laya multilingual
              (ModernBERT architecture, 22 layers, hidden 768,
               vocab 256,000, 321,908,998 parameters in this checkpoint)

The modifications made in EduJev 1.1 relative to the Laya base checkpoint
consist solely of supervised fine-tuning of the existing weights on a
Chinese/English K-12 short-answer grading dataset. No layers were added,
removed, or structurally altered.

